  "worked_solution": "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the product on the left-hand side must expand to match the right-hand side.\n\nFirst, let's expand the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(cx-8)(x+d) & =c{x}^{2}+cdx-8x-8d \\\\  & =c{x}^{2}+(cd-8)x-8d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we equate the expanded form to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\nc{x}^{2}+(cd-8)x-8d=4{x}^{2}-20x+24.\n$$\n\nNow, we compare the coefficients of corresponding terms.\n\n- Equating the coefficients of ${x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\nc=4.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constant terms, we get\n\n$$\n-8d=24\\,\u21d2\\,d=-3.\n$$\n\nLet's verify that values $c=4$ and $d=-3$ produce the correct linear coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cd-8 & =4\\cdot (-3)-8 \\\\  & =-12-8 \\\\  & =-20\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich matches the coefficient of $x$ on the right-hand side. So, our solution is valid.\n\nFinally, we compute the value of $c+d:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c+d & =4+(-3) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
